# Subagent lots

A **lot** is the set of subagents launched in one wave. Wait until that lot has finished before launching the next one.

- Launch the wave, then stop. Do not add agents while any member of the lot is still running, including when a slot frees.
- A launch that fails with "Too many local subagents" did not start. It is not in the lot. Do not retry it until the current lot has finished.
- Do not poll or interrupt a running agent to make the lot end sooner. End the turn and wait for completion notifications.
- Review and land a finished agent's commit as that agent completes. That is part of the current lot, not the next one.
- Start the next lot only after every agent that actually started has reported completion.

```text
Lot 1: launch A, B, C → stop
A finishes → review A's commit; B and C are still running → do not launch D
B and C finish → lot 1 is done → then launch lot 2
```
